link-escape requested=~/.agents/skills/weather/SKILL.md resolved=~/.openclaw/workspace/skills/weather/SKILL.md\nOpenClaw security audit\nSummary: 6 critical · 5 warn · 1 info\nRun deeper: openclaw security audit --deep\n\nCRITICAL\nsecurity.exposure.open_groups_with_elevated Open groupPolicy with elevated tools enabled\n  Found groupPolicy=\"open\" at:\n- channels.telegram.groupPolicy\nWith tools.elevated enabled, a prompt injection in those rooms can become a high-impact incident.\n  Fix: Set groupPolicy=\"allowlist\" and keep elevated allowlists extremely tight.\nsecurity.exposure.open_groups_with_runtime_or_fs Open groupPolicy with runtime/filesystem tools exposed\n  Found groupPolicy=\"open\" at:\n- channels.telegram.groupPolicy\nRisky tool exposure contexts:\n- agents.defaults (sandbox=off; runtime=[exec, process]; fs=[read, write, edit, apply_patch]; fs.workspaceOnly=false)\n- agents.list.main (sandbox=off; runtime=[exec, process]; fs=[read, write, edit, apply_patch]; fs.workspaceOnly=false)\nPrompt injection in open groups can trigger command/file actions in these contexts.\n  Fix: For open groups, prefer tools.profile=\"messaging\" (or deny group:runtime/group:fs), set tools.fs.workspaceOnly=true, and use agents.defaults.sandbox.mode=\"all\" for exposed agents.\nplugins.code_safety Plugin \"claude-mem\" contains dangerous code patterns\n  Found 6 critical issue(s) in 10 scanned file(s):\n  - [dangerous-exec] Shell command execution detected (child_process) (plugin/scripts/bun-runner.js:51)\n  - [dangerous-exec] Shell command execution detected (child_process) (plugin/scripts/mcp-server.cjs:6)\n  - [dynamic-code-execution] Dynamic code execution detected (plugin/scripts/mcp-server.cjs:6)\n  - [env-harvesting] Environment variable access combined with network send — possible credential harvesting (plugin/scripts/mcp-server.cjs:57)\n  - [dangerous-exec] Shell command execution detected (child_process) (plugin/scripts/smart-install.js:78)\n  - [env-harvesting] Environment variable access combined with network send — possible credential harvesting (plugin/scripts/worker-cli.js:5)\n  Fix: Review the plugin source code carefully before use. If untrusted, remove the plugin from your OpenClaw extensions state directory.\nskills.code_safety Skill \"tavily\" contains dangerous code patterns\n  Found 2 critical issue(s) in 2 scanned file(s) under /home/lfant/.openclaw/workspace/skills/tavily-search:\n  - [env-harvesting] Environment variable access combined with network send — possible credential harvesting (scripts/extract.mjs:25)\n  - [env-harvesting] Environment variable access combined with network send — possible credential harvesting (scripts/search.mjs:49)\n  Fix: Review the skill source code before use. If untrusted, remove \"/home/lfant/.openclaw/workspace/skills/tavily-search\".\nskills.code_safety Skill \"writing-skills\" contains dangerous code patterns\n  Found 1 critical issue(s) in 1 scanned file(s) under /home/lfant/.agents/skills/writing-skills:\n  - [dangerous-exec] Shell command execution detected (child_process) (render-graphs.js:25)\n  Fix: Review the skill source code before use. If untrusted, remove \"/home/lfant/.agents/skills/writing-skills\".\nchannels.telegram.warning.1 Telegram security warning\n  Telegram groups: groupPolicy=\"open\" with no channels.telegram.groups allowlist; any group can add + ping (mention-gated). Set channels.telegram.groupPolicy=\"allowlist\" + channels.telegram.groupAllowFrom or configure channels.telegram.groups.\n\nWARN\ngateway.trusted_proxies_missing Reverse proxy headers are not trusted\n  gateway.bind is loopback and gateway.trustedProxies is empty. If you expose the Control UI through a reverse proxy, configure trusted proxies so local-client checks cannot be spoofed.\n  Fix: Set gateway.trustedProxies to your proxy IPs or keep the Control UI local-only.\ntools.exec.auto_allow_skills_enabled autoAllowSkills is enabled for exec approvals\n  Implicit skill-bin allowlisting is enabled at:\n- defaults.autoAllowSkills\nThis widens host exec trust beyond explicit manual allowlist entries.\n  Fix: Disable autoAllowSkills in exec approvals and keep manual allowlists tight when you need explicit host-exec trust.\nsecurity.trust_model.multi_user_heuristic Potential multi-user setup detected (personal-assistant model warning)\n  Heuristic signals indicate this gateway may be reachable by multiple users:\n- channels.telegram.groupPolicy=\"open\"\nRuntime/process tools are exposed without full sandboxing in at least one context.\nPotential high-impact tool exposure contexts:\n- agents.defaults (sandbox=off; runtime=[exec, process]; fs=[read, write, edit, apply_patch]; fs.workspaceOnly=false)\n- agents.list.main (sandbox=off; runtime=[exec, process]; fs=[read, write, edit, apply_patch]; fs.workspaceOnly=false)\nOpenClaw's default security model is personal-assistant (one trusted operator boundary), not hostile multi-tenant isolation on one shared gateway.\n  Fix: If users may be mutually untrusted, split trust boundaries (separate gateways + credentials, ideally separate OS users/hosts). If you intentionally run shared-user access, set agents.defaults.sandbox.mode=\"all\", keep tools.fs.workspaceOnly=true, deny runtime/fs/web tools unless required, and keep personal/private identities + credentials off that runtime.\nplugins.allow_phantom_entries plugins.allow contains entries with no matching installed plugin\n  The following plugins.allow entries do not correspond to any installed plugin: telegram, memory-core, zai, openai, openrouter, ollama.\nPhantom entries could be exploited by registering a new plugin with an allowlisted ID.\n  Fix: Remove unused entries from plugins.allow, or verify the expected plugins are installed.\nplugins.tools_reachable_permissive_policy Extension plugin tools may be reachable under permissive tool policy\n  Enabled extension plugins: claude-mem.\nPermissive tool policy contexts:\n- default\n- agents.list.main\n  Fix: Use restrictive profiles (`minimal`/`coding`) or explicit tool allowlists that exclude plugin tools for agents handling untrusted input.\n\nINFO\nsummary.attack_surface Attack surface summary\n  groups: open=1, allowlist=0\ntools.elevated: enabled\nhooks.webhooks: disabled\nhooks.internal: enabled\nbrowser control: enabled\ntrust model: personal assistant (one trusted operator boundary), not hostile multi-tenant on one shared gateway\n","name":"openclaw security"},"isError":false,"timestamp":1777053634556}}
{"type":"message","id":"a7e29146","parentId":"9f36e2b3","timestamp":"2026-04-24T18:01:28.313Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"보안 감사 완료했습니다. 오탐으로 지정된 항목을 제외한 실제 보안 이슈를 요약합니다.\n\n---\n\n## 보안 감사 결과 요약\n\n### CRITICAL (3건)\n\n#### 1. Open Group Policy with Elevated Tools\n**위치:** `channels.telegram.groupPolicy = \"open\"`\n\n**문제:**\n- 열려 있는 그룹에서 `tools.elevated`가 활성화되어 있음\n- 프롬프트 인젝션 공격 시 고위험 이슈 발생 가능\n\n**권장 조치:**\n```yaml\nchannels:\n  telegram:\n    groupPolicy: \"allowlist\"\n    # 또는 tools.profile: \"messaging\" 사용\n```\n\n---\n\n#### 2. Open Group Policy with Runtime/Filesystem Tools\n**위치:** `channels.telegram.groupPolicy = \"open\"`\n\n**문제:**\n- 열려 있는 그룹에서 runtime/process 및 파일 시스템 도구 노출\n- `agents.defaults`와 `agents.list.main`에서 샌드박스 비활성화 상태\n\n**권장 조치:**\n```yaml\nagents:\n  defaults:\n    sandbox:\n      mode: \"all\"  # 샌드박스 활성화\ntools:\n  fs:\n    workspaceOnly: true\n```\n\n---\n\n#### 3. Telegram Group Allowlist Missing\n**위치:** `channels.telegram.groupPolicy = \"open\"`\n\n**문제:**\n- `groupPolicy`가 \"open\"이지만 `groupAllowFrom` allowlist가 없음\n- 모든 그룹에서 봇을 추가하고 멘션 가능\n\n**권한 조치:**\n```yaml\nchannels:\n  telegram:\n    groupPolicy: \"allowlist\"\n    groupAllowFrom: \n      - \"그룹ID1\"\n      - \"그룹ID2\"\n```\n\n---\n\n### WARN (5건)\n\n#### 1. Gateway Trusted Proxies Missing\n**문제:** Reverse proxy 사용 시 `trustedProxies` 미설정\n\n**조치:**\n```yaml\ngateway:\n  trustedProxies: \n    - \"프록시IP\"\n```\n\n---\n\n#### 2. autoAllowSkills Enabled\n**위치:** `defaults.autoAllowSkills = true`\n\n**문제:** 스킬 자동 허용으로 실행 권한이 느슨함\n\n**조치:** 수동 allowlist 사용 권장\n\n---\n\n#### 3. Multi-User Setup Warning\n**문제:** 여러 사용자가 접근 가능한 환경에서 샌드박스 미활성화\n\n**조치:**\n- 개인 사용자만 접근 시: 현상태 유지 가능\n- 공유 사용 시: `sandbox.mode: \"all\"` + `fs.workspaceOnly: true`\n\n---\n\n#### 4. Phantom Plugin Entries\n**문제:** 설치되지 않은 플러그인이 `plugins.allow`에 있음\n- `telegram, memory-core, zai, openai, openrouter, ollama`\n\n**조치:** 미사용 항목 제거\n\n---\n\n#### 5. Permissive Plugin Tool Policy\n**문제:** 확장 플러그인 도구가 허용적인 정책에서 접근 가능\n\n**조치:** 제한적인 프로필(`minimal`/`coding`) 사용\n\n---\n\n## 오탐 제외 항목 (지정됨)\n\n다음 코드 안전 경고는 오탐으로 처리하고 무시합니다:\n\n- ✅ `tavily-search` skill\n  - `scripts/extract.mjs:25` (env-harvesting)\n  - `scripts/search.mjs:49` (env-harvesting)\n\n- ✅ `claude-mem` plugin\n  - `scripts/bun-runner.js:51` (dangerous-exec)\n  - `scripts/mcp-server.cjs:6` (dangerous-exec, dynamic-code-execution, env-harvesting)\n  - `scripts/smart-install.js:78` (dangerous-exec)\n  - `scripts/worker-cli.js:5` (env-harvesting)\n\n- ✅ `writing-skills` skill\n  - `render-graphs.js:25` (dangerous-exec)\n\n---\n\n## 주요 권장 우선순위\n\n1. **즉시 조치:**\n   - `channels.telegram.groupPolicy` → \"allowlist\" 변경\n   - `groupAllowFrom` allowlist 구성\n\n2. **단기 조치:**\n   - `agents.defaults.sandbox.mode` → \"all\" 설정\n   - `tools.fs.workspaceOnly` → true 설정\n\n3. **중기 조치:**\n   - 미사용 플러그인 항목 정리\n   - `autoAllowSkills` 비활성화\n\n보안 정책은 현재 Personal Assistant 모델(단일 신뢰 운영자)로 설계되어 있으므로, 실제로 단일 사용자만 접근한다면 우선순위를 낮게 조정할 수 있습니다."}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"zai","model":"glm-4.7","usage":{"input":3914,"output":1122,"cacheRead":14370,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":19406,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"stop","timestamp":1777053634559,"responseId":"2026042502003541067a13107d4287"}}
